From 788591b76cb78f7a371bccd98ab7cf5bf7cba735 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ygecesefa <ygecesefa@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:17:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Decrypt /data: qseecomd's listener libraries

qseecomd exited at once (status 255) in the first decryption build:
'Init dlopen(librpmb.so) failed ... RPMB_INIT failed, shall not start
listener services'. Its listeners are dlopen()ed, so they were not in
the readelf closure. Add them (from the strings in qseecomd) and their
dependencies, again from the tablet's vendor: librpmb, libssd, libgpt,
libops, libspl, libqisl, libdrmtime, libGPreqcancel(_svc),
libtime_genoff, libdrm, libdisplayconfig.qti, vendor.display.config@2.0.
libsecureui.so is named too but does not exist on the tablet either.
